  ('2042e8cc-74a0-5b11-be0a-f77eee368da9', '1f5eec05-62c1-5cdd-9071-7d57605fb039', 'e9b492d0-27ae-516c-9fcd-fba6d37040a5', 'Arts::Folklore Studies', 'D152', 'functional', 'audit_sweep_2026-08-17', 'strong', 2, '[{"title":"Research Methods in the Arts","mapping_title":null,"code":"FAC 301","course_identity":"FAC 301::Research Methods in the Arts","matched_anchors":["archive"]},{"title":"Folklore Entrepreneurship","mapping_title":null,"code":"FLS 304","course_identity":"FLS 304::Folklore Entrepreneurship","matched_anchors":["museum"]}]'::jsonb, 1, '[{"evidence":"describe roles of international organisations, media and traditional institutions in peace building Concepts of peace, conflict and security in a multi-ethnic nation. Types and theories of conflicts: ethnic, religious, economic, geo-political conflicts. Structural conflict theory, realist theory of conflict, frustration-aggression conflict theory. Root causes of conflict and violence in Africa: indigene and settlers phenomena; boundary/boarder disputes; political disputes; ethnic disputes and rivalries. Economic inequalities; social dispute. Nationalist movements and agitations. Selected conflict case studies � Tiv-Junkun; Zango Kartaf. Chieftaincy and land disputes, etc. Peace building, management of conflicts and security. Peace and human development. Approaches to eace & conflict management --- (religious, government, community leaders etc.). elements of peace studies and conflict resolution. Conflict dynamics assessment scales. Constructive and destructive, justice and legal framework. Concepts of social justice; the Nigerian legal system. Insurgency and terrorism. Peace mediation and peace keeping. Peace and Security Council (international, national and local levels). Agents of conflict resolution � conventions, treaties, community policing. evolution and imperatives. Alternative New Arts 283 Dispute Resolution (ADR). Dialogue, arbitration, negotiation, collaboration, etc. Roles of international organizations in conflict resolution - (a). the United Nations (UN) and its conflict resolution organs; the African Union and Peace Security Council. ECOWAS in peace keeping. The media and traditional institutions in peace building. Managing post-conflict situations; refugees. Internally Displaced Persons (IDPS). The role of NGOs in post-conflict situations","categories":["planning_and_delivery","collaboration_and_leadership"]}]'::jsonb, false, false, '{"ccmas_source_file":"arts.json","ccmas_code":"FLS","qualification":"B.Sc","duration_years":4,"domain_name":"Museum Curation, Cultural Heritage, Archives","domain_definition":"Museum curation, cultural heritage and archives work protects and organises a society''s art, objects and records. Curators plan collections and exhibitions, art restorers repair damaged works, and librarians and archivists manage information, from physical documents to digital archives. Museums, galleries, libraries and cultural institutions provide most of the work.","audit_source":"programme_domain_evidence_2026-08-17","source_flagged_courses":[],"programme_source_flags":[],"adjacent_evidence_gate":null}'::jsonb),
